                <head>210. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On June 28 Ambassador Young sent an airgram
                    to the Department of State evaluating the current state of U.S.-Dutch relations.
                    He suggested that with the establishment of the J.E. deQuay Cabinet, which had
                    been formed on May 19, the time had come “when we should take [a] fresh, overall
                    look at our relations with the Dutch.” (Airgram G–193 from The Hague, June 28; Department of State, Central Files,
                    611.56/6–2859) See Supplement.</p>
            </div>
